Student Project Catalog Portal
Access Control & Permission Requirements

1. Overview

The Student Project Catalog Portal implements role-based access control to ensure that students and administrators can access only the features and operations permitted for their roles.

The system has two primary roles:

- Student: Can browse projects, request projects, download approved projects, submit community projects, manage their own submissions, and review downloaded projects.
- Admin: Has overall system management privileges, including official project management, community submission reviews, request approvals, user management, and content moderation.

All role-based and ownership-based authorization checks must be enforced at the API level.



2. User Roles

2.1 Student

- Default role assigned when a new user registers.
- Can browse official and approved community projects.
- Can search, filter, and sort projects.
- Can request projects created by other users.
- Can download projects after request approval.
- Can submit their own community projects.
- Can manage their own project submissions.
- Can view their requests, downloads, and submissions.
- Can rate and review projects after downloading them.
- Can report projects or reviews that violate platform rules.
- Cannot access administrator-only functionalities.

2.2 Admin

- Has access to the protected administrator panel.
- Can create and publish official projects.
- Can create community projects.
- Can edit any project.
- Can delete or deactivate projects.
- Can review and approve community submissions.
- Can reject submissions with a mandatory reason.
- Can request changes to community submissions.
- Can unpublish approved community projects.
- Can manage student project requests.
- Can approve or reject project requests.
- Can manage users and their posting status.
- Can warn or ban students from posting after repeated violations.
- Can handle reports submitted by students.
- Can moderate project reviews.
- Can access project statistics and platform insights.



3. Authentication and Access Security

3.1 User Registration

- Visitors can register using their name, email, and password.
- Email addresses must be unique.
- Passwords must be hashed before storage.
- Every newly registered account must receive the Student role by default.

3.2 User Login

- Users must authenticate before accessing protected features.
- Incorrect credentials must display a clear error message.
- Repeated login failures must be rate-limited.
- The system must use secure token-based sessions.

3.3 User Logout

- Users must be able to log out securely.
- Logout must protect accounts when users access the application from shared computers.

3.4 Password Reset

- Users must be able to reset forgotten passwords through email.
- Password reset links must expire quickly.
- Each reset link must work only once.
- Reset tokens must be stored as hashes.

3.5 Protected Pages

- Unauthenticated users attempting to access protected pages must be redirected to the login page.
- Private user information must not be accessible to unauthorized users.
- The admin panel must be protected using role-based authorization.

3.6 API Security

- Role and ownership checks must be enforced at the API level.
- Students attempting to access administrator-only endpoints must receive HTTP 403 Forbidden.
- All inputs must be sanitized.
- Password hashes and password-reset fields must never be returned in API responses.



4. Project Access Permissions

4.1 Official Projects

- Only administrators can create official projects.
- Official projects must be published immediately with the Official badge.
- Administrators can edit official projects.
- Administrators can delete or deactivate any project.
- Students can browse and request official projects.

4.2 Community Projects

- Students can submit their own projects as community projects.
- Administrators can also create community projects.
- Students must confirm that the submitted work belongs to them or that they have the right to share it.
- Students must accept the terms agreement before submission.
- Community submissions must initially enter the Pending Review status.
- Only approved community projects can become publicly available.
- Administrators can approve, reject, or request changes to submissions.
- Administrators can unpublish community projects after approval.

4.3 Project Ownership

- Students can edit only projects where the `createdBy` field matches their own user ID.
- Administrators can edit any project.
- Students can withdraw or delete only their own projects.
- Administrators can deactivate any project.
- Deleting a project must use soft deletion by setting `isActive = false`.
- Project documents must not be physically removed because existing requests and downloads must remain valid.
- Editing a published community project must return it to Pending Review for re-approval.

4.4 Public Project Visibility

A project must be publicly visible only when both conditions are satisfied:

- submissionStatus = approved
- isActive = true

Projects that are pending review, rejected, inactive, or awaiting changes must not appear in public project listings.



5. Project Request Permissions

5.1 Student Permissions

- Only logged-in students can request projects.
- Students can request projects created by other users.
- Students cannot request their own projects.
- Students cannot create duplicate active requests for the same project.
- Active requests include Pending and Approved requests.
- Students can view their own request statuses.
- Students can view rejection reasons.
- Students can download projects only after approval.

5.2 Admin Permissions

- Administrators can view all project requests.
- Administrators can view the student, project, request note, status, and request date.
- Administrators can filter requests by status and project source.
- Administrators can approve project requests.
- Administrators can reject project requests with a mandatory reason.
- Administrators can review and manage request statuses.
- Requests must be marked as Delivered after a successful download.

5.3 Request Status Flow

- Pending → Approved → Delivered
- Pending → Rejected

Every request status change must trigger an email notification.

5.4 Request Approval Delegation

As an optional stretch feature, administrators may delegate request approval for a community project to its author.

The decidedBy field can identify the administrator or delegated project author who made the decision.



6. Download Access Permissions

- Project downloads must be restricted to authorized students.
- A student must have an Approved or Delivered request to download a project.
- Downloads must remain blocked before approval.
- The API must enforce download authorization.
- Download links must expire after a short time.
- A fresh download link must be generated whenever required.
- Download links must never be stored as permanent public links.
- The system must store the private storage ID of the ZIP file.
- The first successful download must update the request to Delivered.
- Download counts must be maintained.



7. Community Submission Review Permissions

Student Permissions

- Students can submit their own projects.
- Students can save submissions as drafts.
- Students can view their submission status.
- Students can read administrator feedback.
- Students can edit their own submissions.
- Students can resubmit projects after making requested changes.
- Students can withdraw or delete their own projects.

Admin Permissions

- Administrators can view the pending submission review queue.
- Administrators can preview submission details, screenshots, and ZIP files.
- Administrators can approve submissions.
- Administrators can reject submissions only when a rejection reason is provided.
- Administrators can request changes with specific feedback.
- Administrators can unpublish community projects.
- Administrators can moderate submissions that violate platform rules.

Submission Status Flow

Draft → Pending Review → Approved

Other possible transitions:

- Pending Review → Rejected
- Pending Review → Changes Requested
- Changes Requested → Pending Review (after student edits and resubmits)

Only approved submissions become publicly available.



8. Review and Rating Permissions

Student Permissions

- Students can review a project only after successfully downloading it.
- Students cannot review their own projects.
- Each student can submit only one review per project.
- Students can edit or delete their own reviews.
- Ratings must be between 1 and 5.
- Students can report inappropriate or rule-breaking reviews.

Admin Permissions

- Administrators can moderate project reviews.
- Administrators can hide inappropriate reviews.
- Administrators can manage reported reviews.

Review Authorization Rules

- A user must have a Delivered request for the project before submitting a review.
- The reviewer must not be the project's author.
- A unique constraint must exist on `userId + projectId`.
- Project rating statistics must be recalculated after review creation, editing, deletion, or hiding.



9. Reporting and Moderation Permissions

Student Permissions

Students can report:

- Projects containing plagiarized code.
- Projects containing malware.
- Inappropriate projects or reviews.
- Content containing personal data.
- Other content that violates platform rules.

Admin Permissions

Administrators can:

- View and handle student reports.
- Resolve or dismiss reports.
- Moderate reported projects and reviews.
- Warn students after repeated violations.
- Ban students from posting after repeated violations.

Posting Restrictions

The user posting status can have three values:

- active
- warned
- banned

A banned student:

- Can still browse projects.
- Can still request projects.
- Cannot submit new projects.



10. User Management Permissions

Student Permissions

- Students can edit their own profiles.
- Students can change their passwords.
- Students can view their own requests.
- Students can view their own downloads.
- Students can view and manage their own submissions.

Admin Permissions

- Administrators can access the user list.
- Administrators can view user roles.
- Administrators can view user join dates.
- Administrators can view user posting statuses.
- Administrators can manage student posting restrictions.
- Administrators can warn or ban students after repeated violations.



11. Admin Dashboard and Insights Permissions

Only administrators can access the administrative statistics and insights features.

Administrators can view:

- Total official projects.
- Total community projects.
- Community submissions grouped by status.
- Project requests grouped by status.
- Top courses.
- Top contributors.
- Contributor activity.

Administrators can also moderate reviews to maintain trustworthy project ratings.



12. Complete Permission Summary

The following table represents the permission summary specified in Section 4.9 of the requirements document.

| Action                        | Student                  | Admin               |
|    -    -    -    -    -    - |   -   -   -   -   -   -  |   -   -   -   -   - |
| Create official project       | No                       | Yes (auto-approved) |
| Create community project      | Yes (needs review)       | Yes                 |
| Edit a project                | Only their own           | Any                 |
| Approve or reject submissions | No                       | Yes                 |
| Request a project             | Yes (not their own)      | Not applicable      |
| Approve or reject requests    | No (optional delegation) | Yes                 |
| Review a project              | Only after download      | Moderate only       |



13. Security and Quality Requirements

The following system-level requirements must be enforced:

| ID | Requirement 

| Q1 | List endpoints must respond in under 500 ms. 
| Q2 | Login attempts must be rate-limited and all inputs sanitized. 
| Q3 | Uploads must be restricted by file type and size and checked where possible. 
| Q4 | Download links must expire after a short time. 
| Q5 | Role and ownership checks must be enforced in the API. 
| Q6 | Only approved and active projects must appear in public listings. 
| Q7 | Jest and Supertest API tests, along with one Playwright end-to-end test, must cover the complete flow: submit, review, request, approve, and download. 

Mandatory Authorization Test Cases

- A student must not access administrator-only endpoints.
- A student must not edit another student's project.
- A student must not request their own project.
- A student must not download a project before approval.
- A student must not review a project before downloading it.
- A banned student must not submit projects.
- An unauthenticated user must not access protected pages.
- Only approved and active projects must appear in public listings.



14. Implementation Priority

The following access-control-related requirements are included in the Must-have scope:

- Student and administrator role separation.
- Secure authentication and token-based sessions.
- Protected administrator endpoints.
- Project ownership verification.
- Approval-based community publishing.
- Approval-based project downloads.
- Request authorization.
- Review eligibility validation.
- User posting restrictions.
- API-level role and ownership checks.

The following are optional stretch features:

- Delegated request approval for community project authors (A26).
- Warning and ban system (A15 is a must-have admin story, but the ban system is identified as a feature that may be deferred if the 12-week scope becomes too large).



